.TH SDL_HINT_ASSERT 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_ASSERT \- A variable controlling response to
.BR SDL_assert
failures.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_ASSERT \(dqSDL_ASSERT\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following case-sensitive values:
.PP

\(bu \(dqabort\(dq: Program terminates immediately\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqbreak\(dq: Program triggers a debugger breakpoint\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqretry\(dq: Program reruns the
.BR SDL_assert \(aqs
test again\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqignore\(dq: Program continues on, ignoring this assertion failure this time\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqalways_ignore\(dq: Program continues on, ignoring this assertion failure for the rest of the run\[char46]
.PP
Note that
.BR SDL_SetAssertionHandler
offers a programmatic means to deal with assertion failures through a callback, and this hint is largely intended to be used via environment variables by end users and automated tools\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before an assertion failure is triggered and can be changed at any time\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

